# A CONTROL, NEVER A CUT OF THE PRODUCT (2026-10-17, frame generation phase 5, package F3: the position t in the library).
# The cut fi-position makes the generated frame's place between the two real frames a constant of the dispatch, and at
# the middle (0.5, what every caller asks on 2026-10-17) the judge must find AMD's picture in every pair. That proves
# the cut exact only if the constant REACHES the shaders: a constant that never arrived would give the middle too. This
# is the library that asks for another place: our glue, where the caller says the middle (position 0), tells AMD's
# dispatch 0.4. Everything after the glue is the exact library's: the same clamp, the same field of AMD's dispatch
# description, the same spare word, the same shaders. Built on the exact library's cuts (build-ffx-own.ps1 -Target
# dlssiv-fg -Cuts exact,+control-position -OutDir obj\dlssiv-fg-pos); tools\test-fg-own\run.py --ours (step 6c) must
# find it DIFFERENT from AMD's on every arm whose picture moves (F, FK, F1, FN, FC), and it may equal AMD's only where t
# cannot show: a reset pair (the current picture is copied) and an arm where nothing moves.
what THE JUDGE'S CONTROL OF fi-position: the glue tells AMD's dispatch the position 0.4 where the caller says the middle
passes none
wave64 it changes our glue alone; it is a control and is never in the product
